{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let $x$ represent the unknown cost of $6$ pencils. Since $6$ pencils cost $x$, we have the following proportion:","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\qquad \\dfrac{6}{x}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We can write the fact that $9$ pencils cost $\\$7.74$ as a proportion:","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\qquad \\dfrac{9}{\\$7.74}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The cost changes along with the number of pencils purchased, and so the two proportions are equivalent.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\qquad \\dfrac{6}{x} = \\dfrac{9}{\\$7.74}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$9$ pencils cost $\\$7.74$. \n\n** Which equation would help determine the cost of $6$ pencils? **\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{6}{x} = \\dfrac{9}{\\$7.74}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac{x}{6} = \\dfrac{9}{\\$7.74}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{9}{6} = \\dfrac{x}{\\$7.74}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{6}{x} = \\dfrac{\\$7.74}{9}$","correct":false},{"content":"None of the above","correct":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
